@meta
id: 09-03
title: Drill — the doubled word
chapter: 09
type: drill
skills: op-motion
par: 11
minutes: 4
reps: 8
vscode: double-click, Backspace, Backspace
open: orders.md

@brief
Eight times: delete the second `are`, save, quit. Nothing to think about.

`dw` should become one gesture rather than two decisions.

@keys
| `3w` | three words forward |
| `dw` | delete from here to the start of the next word |

@hints
Count the words on the way in rather than pressing `w` three times.
--
`3w` then `dw`. Four keys before the colon.

@solution
    3w dw :wq<Enter>

Eight keystrokes, and after a few reps your hand stops spelling it out.

There is a faster answer here — `d3w` from the first `are` deletes three
words at once, and if the duplication were a whole phrase that is what you
would reach for. It is not faster for one word, and reaching for it here
would mean counting under pressure. Counting when you do not have to is
how people end up deleting one word too many.

